{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1465647-i-just-don-t-understand-how-to-run-a-changeling-game","id":1465647,"title":"I just don't understand how to run a Changeling game.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-10-28T07:23:33-07:00","id":1465647,"title":"I just don't understand how to run a Changeling game.","content":"I've been running Werewolf games for quite awhile now. I've also run a Vampire game and a Technocracy game. I've read the Changeling book, and immediately fell in love with the aesthetics of the game, as well as the concept of fighting against Banality. I run into a problem though whenever I try to plan a chronicle though. I have no idea how to run a Changeling game and what to have my players even do.<br /> <br /> Werewolf is easy. You have a very obvious enemy to fight, that come in a variety of flavors to keep things fresh. You also have some of the internal Sept politics or conflicts with other Septs to sprinkle in as well. Vampire I also found easy. It's just political games in order to gain hard and soft power using humanity as pawns a lot of the time. They also have very obvious enemies as there are three distinct factions between the Camarilla, Sabbat and Anarchs. Changeling though, I just don't get what it is they're doing most of the time. Conflict between the Seelie, Unseelie and Shadow Courts seem to be the biggest problem Changelings face with their darker enemies like the Thallain sounding like it's a rarer occurance. Unlike Vampire though, it doesn't sound like most Changelings get involved in deep politics as most Changelings are just commoners doing their own thing. And the ones that do get political, I don't even understand what their goals would be.<br /> <br /> I don't know if it's because Changelings basically live in the real world and Chimerical world at the same time, but I really struggle to come up with a cohesive story that has real stakes and can blend action/intrigue and give my players a solid antagonist. I'm hoping someone here might be able to help me out in understand what exactly Changeling is supposed to look like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T09:10:34-07:00","id":1465663,"title":"","content":"There are a few avenues you can work it for starters. It is actually a very versatile game.<br /> <br /> We can broadly divide them in <b>Politics</b>, <b>Survival</b>, <b>Nightmare</b>, <b>Rescue </b>and <b>Adventure</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>Politics - </b>Changelings dispute influence and resources, but without so much of the personal hoarding theme of vampires. Instead they're more similar to real world politics. Everyone have problems and expect their government be able to address those problems, everyone have their ideologies and vision for the future.<br /> <br /> A Changeling political game can focus on nobles, but commoners frequently have an invested interest and not all of them are alienated from the dealings in the Courts. Members of a Household spy and traffic information, rebels organize in secret, demagogues on all sides try to sway public opinion.<br /> <br /> More importantly, secrecy is as far less pressing concern for Changelings, like far, far less. So when things get ugly, they get ugly.<br /> <br /> <b>Survival - </b>Depending on how you set the overall Banality of your setting, things are bleak for Changelings. Places and people with High Banality scores may be everywhere and cause a lot of trouble, making Freeholds absolutely vital for safety. But also limited in supply.<br /> <br /> In this kind of game the PCs must secure resources and safe places, and be always on their toes for rivals and disaster, as Changelings can't always do much about the flux of Glamour and Banality.<br /> <br /> Things get even more dare when you split the resources needed for each side of their lives. They're still human and need food, shelter, health care and so on. But they can't always get those things in low Banality areas.<br /> <br /> <b>Nightmare - </b>Thallain, Dark Kin and other threats aren't a constant, but when they arrive it isn't just for the weekend. The same goes for any other external enemy, be them Prodigals, Gallain, powerful Chimera or whatever. A Changeling territory besieged by enemies may have a long term situation to deal with.<br /> <br /> It is important to say that Changelings aren't necessarily affected by evil in any special way. They don't have either a Beast nor Humanity, there is no Gaia or Wyrm, what keeps Changelings from becoming monsters isn't any law or rule, just the will of other Changelings to be heroes. But when things start to kill their sources of Glamour, then it stops being an option and becomes a need to fight the darkness.<br /> <br /> <b>Rescue - </b>Changelings have a strong sense of duty to bring one another from the brink of true destruction. And they suffer quite a few very serious risks to their existences that can offer a lot of challenge to wannabe rescuers at the same time.<br /> <br /> Bedlam and Banality are the best examples, as they both can make a Changeling very dangerous to their peers. A Banal Changeling can cause the same effects of a Banal person, up to and including raising the local Banality of their homes to a level dangerous to others. They are also Banal for a reason, and so probably aren't easy to reach without going near sources of high Banality, even Autumn People. If you get there, helping them get rid of Banality when they're already so close to being Undone is also very challenging.<br /> <br /> And one at Bedlam is erratic. Worse, they make the Dream lash out around them one way or another. Wild chimeras, uncontrolled Arts, a risk of contagion, all that adds to the danger of a delirious Fae that can become hostile for reasons people around them can't quite comprehend (they should exist and make sense, though, just not be seen by others).<br /> <br /> <b>Adventure - </b>Finally, Changelings love to just find shit to do. Journey in search of arcane ingredients for a patron, or a fallen star for a loved one, picking fights for honor or being bound to pledges, they usually are very active on their own, nobility or not, they are used to drama and grandiose actions, they seek creativity as much as they are creative and live creatively.<br /> <br /> There is no excess of drama when Changelings are around, or the cold grasp of Banality will manifest itself. Exact pledges, throw parties, make messes. A pledge sworn under the effects of alcohol or the Satyr's <i>Gift of Pan</i> is as valid or more than one pledged when completely sober. Have things go wrong just due to imprudence and impulsivity of someone. A Changeling is as likely to run from a Garou on Crinos as it is to hit on the Garou then and there for some sweet love. And drop the consequences on the party's back.<br /> <br /> And for a lot of situations you'll find the suggestion of Quests. Needs some medicine? A Quest. Dropping Banality? A Quest. Want answer to a question? Quest. Low on Glamour and no Dreamer nearby? Quest. Nothing to do this afternoon? Quest. To make or break a Pledge, lift curses, find the secret KFC recipe, you can go after anything on a Quest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T10:22:52-07:00","id":1465667,"title":"","content":"What I generally try to do with Changeling is lean a bit more into the double-life that most Kithain have to lead. Start off by focusing on their mundane troubles and the conflicts those create with their fae existence. Likewise when dealing with Changeling politics focus on the problems it causes to spill over into their normal lives. I'd actually recommend Hunter: the Reckoning for some good advice and resources on this front. <br /> <br /> I also like to use Chimera as antagonists and plot-initiators. They can be as bizarre or even horrifying as you need them to be, since they come from the depths of our collective unconscious. You can get some good monster of the week action from them in this regard. They also have the virtue of being apolitical, so they cut across rank and court and can be used to mix up those dynamics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T03:33:05-07:00","id":1465995,"title":"","content":"Honestly if you've run Werewolf then Changeling shouldn't be too hard of a pivot.<br /> <br /> There is a Household ( Sept) setup, usually, within a Freehold ( Caern), there are leadership positions within the Household such as Seer, Jester, Steward etc. ( Warder, Master of the Challenge etc.)<br /> <br /> Much of the day to day routine is seeing to relations between other Households, Managing the local Chimera ( Spirits), defending the Freehold against Prodigals ( Vampires, Mages), going on quests, recovering Treasures ( Fetishes) etc.<br /> <br /> I mean there are also some fairly major differences but you've already got a good basis to build from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T05:25:49-07:00","id":1466000,"title":"","content":"And don\u2019t forget Romance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T10:06:01-07:00","id":1466029,"title":"","content":"I think my friend may have Liked my post above so if that\u2019s you Hey girl!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Amethyst is my birthstone. She/they.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26996-amethyst","name":"Amethyst","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"873"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-09T06:45:20-08:00","id":1467255,"title":"","content":"Thanks to everyone who responded. It's given me some ways to think about the game that didn't occur to me at first","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7550-vulcan7200","name":"Vulcan7200","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}